stability-boost-14ede736.conceptual_definition:
This formula, titled 'Stability Boost,' describes the total effective pressure (
$P_{tot}$
) within a system as the sum of two contributing components: the degeneracy pressure (
$P_{deg}$
) and the strong nuclear force pressure (
$P_{strong}$
). It is particularly relevant in contexts where quantum mechanical effects and nuclear interactions play a significant role in maintaining the stability and structure of matter, such as in white dwarf stars or neutron stars.
